# DNAseq conda environments

Makefile and definitions for the `DNAseq_R`, `DNAseq_Tools` and
`DNAseq_Python` conda environments.

`DNAseq_R` gets its R packages from conda (`DNAseq_R.yaml`). It then updates
them, and installs the GitHub-only packages in `PackagesToInstall.txt`. The
build scripts and recipes are shared with the other environments. They live in
`../R_build_common/` (see the README there).

## Files

1. `Makefile`: environment-specific targets (run `make help`).
1. `DNAseq_R.yaml`, `DNAseq_Tools.yaml`, `DNAseq_Python.yaml`: conda
   environment definitions.
1. `PackagesToInstall.txt`: GitHub R packages to install.

## Usage

```bash
make            # everything
make create-r   # R environment and R package steps only
make help       # list targets
```

`make` runs `create-env`, `create-tools-env`, `create-python-env`,
`update-packages`, `install-packages` and `check-logs`. If `check-logs` finds
a `FAILURE` it exits with an error and keeps `AllPackageInstallationLogs/` and
`AllPackageInstallationSummary.log` for review. Otherwise the logs are
removed.
